==History==
2016
*The Inferno Dragon [[Cards|card]] was added to the game on 30/9/2016.
*On 1/11/2016, the [[Version History#November 2016 Update (1/11/2016)|November 2016 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Inferno Dragon from P.E.K.K.A's Playhouse to Frozen Peak. However, Supercell confirmed on Reddit that this change was unintentional. This change was reverted the next day, on 2/11/2016, in a [[Version History#Maintenance Break (2/11/2016)|maintenance break]].
*On 15/12/2016, the [[Version History#December 2016 Update (15/12/2016)|December 2016 Update]] increased the Inferno Dragon's hitpoints by 5% and decreased its re-targeting time by 0.4 seconds.
2017
*On 13/3/2017, the [[Version History#March%202017%20Update%20(13/3/2017)|March 2017 Update]], added the audience sound effects when the Inferno Dragon is deployed.
*On 12/6/2017, the [[Version History#June 2017 Update (12/6/2017)|June 2017 Update]], increased the Inferno Dragon's hitpoints by 7%, and decreased its re-targeting time by 0.2 seconds.
*On 9/10/2017, the [[Version History#Epic Quests Update (9/10/2017)|Epic Quests Update]], fixed a bug where the Inferno Dragon's damage did not reset after breaking a shield. This change was reverted on 11/10/2017, in a [[Version History#Maintenance%20Break%20(11/10/2017)|maintenance break]].
*On 12/12/2017, the [[Version History#Electrifying Update (12/12/2017)|Electrifying Update]], reverted the Inferno Dragon to its state on 9/10/2017. More specifically, the Inferno Dragon's damage would now reset after breaking a shield.
2018
*On 12/2/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (12/2/2018)|Balance Update]], increased the Inferno Dragon’s re-targeting time by 0.2 seconds.
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Inferno Dragon from P.E.K.K.A's Playhouse to Builder's Workshop.
*On 6/8/2018, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/8/2018)|Balance Update]], decreased the Inferno Dragon's range to 3.5 tiles (from 4 tiles) and allowed it to be knocked back.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Legendary}} cards start at Level 9 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 5).
2020
*On 28/5/2020, a maintenance break, added a card render to the Inferno Dragon's card info screen.
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Inferno Dragon from Builder's Workshop to Jungle Arena.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13).
2022
*On 26/10/2022, the [[Version History#2022%20Quarter%203%20Update%20(26/10/2022)|2022 Quarter 3 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Inferno Dragon from Jungle Arena to Electro Valley.
2023
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14).
2025
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2024)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], increased the Inferno Dragon's hitpoints by 0.07%.
*On 2/6/2025, the [[Version History#Pass Royale and more (2/6/2025)|June 2025 Update]], added the Inferno Dragon's Evolution.

