==Trivia==
*The Inferno Dragon resembles [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/European_dragon dragons from European cultures]. being reptilian legendary creatures, often depicted as winged, horned, and capable of breathing fire.
**The Inferno Dragon is of the same breed as the [[Baby Dragon]], but the Inferno Dragon moves slower, and has slightly more hitpoints, possibly because it carries extra equipment and wears a helmet. However, they are otherwise identical in terms of animations and deployment sound effects.
**A Trainer in the [[Training Camp]] is called Trainer Dragon and uses 2 dragon [[cards]] in their [[Battle Decks|deck]], one of them being Inferno Dragon, and the other being Baby Dragon.
*The word "''Inferno''" comes from the Latin "''inferus''", meaning underworld.
**In the French, Turkish, Chinese, Persian, and Malaysian language settings of the game, the Inferno Dragon's name translates to "Hell Dragon". In the Portuguese language settings of the game, the Inferno Dragon's name translates to "Infernal Dragon". In the Russian and Arabic language settings of the game, the Inferno Dragon's name translates to "Fiery Dragon".
*The Inferno Dragon is 1 of 17 [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] that inspired a troop in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Spear Goblins]], [[Bomber]], [[Bats]], [[Skeleton Barrel]], [[Minion Horde]], [[Firecracker]], [[Battle Ram]], [[Ice Golem]], [[Zappies]], Baby Dragon, [[Giant Skeleton]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Miner]], [[Royal Ghost]], [[Ice Wizard]], and [[Night Witch]].
**The Inferno Dragon's card render is shared with Clash of Clans. Despite coming after the one in Clash Royale, the artwork was originally made for Clash of Clans.
**The barrel on its back likely contains Dark Elixir, as it is the source of fuel for the Inferno Tower in Clash of Clans, and Dark Elixir is also needed to obtain an Inferno Dragon in that game.
*The Inferno Dragon is tied with the [[Mighty Miner]] and the [[Little Prince]] for the highest attack speed of all troops, with an attack speed of 0.4 seconds.
*The Inferno Dragon is 1 of 4 troops that has been featured in the [[Treasure Hunt#Dragon Hunt|Dragon Hunt]] sub-[[:Category:Modes|mode]] of the [[Treasure Hunt]] game mode, the others being [[Skeleton Dragons]], Baby Dragon, and [[Electro Dragon]].
*The Inferno Dragon is 1 of 15 troops which bring an excited reaction from the audience upon spawning and brings a collective groan from the audience when defeated, as well as a concerning gasp when the opponent plays it, the others include [[Royal Giant]], [[Giant]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], Giant Skeleton, [[Rune Giant]], [[Goblin Giant]], [[Golem]], [[Bowler]], [[Electro Wizard]], [[Sparky]], [[Lava Hound]], Night Witch, [[Super Lava Hound]], and the [[Monk]].
*Acoording to the [https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=4M_PPPCN19E Electro Dragon's intro video], it is implied that the Baby Dragon, [[Electro Dragon]], and Inferno Dragon are brothers.
*The Inferno Dragon, along with the [[Minions]], Bomber, [[Skeletons]], Skeleton Dragons, [[Ice Spirit]], [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Mega Minion]], Ice Golem, [[Dart Goblin]], [[Elixir Golem]], [[Goblin Cage|Goblin Brawler]], [[Guards]], Baby Dragon, P.E.K.K.A, Giant Skeleton, Golem, [[Wall Breakers]], Bowler, [[Executioner]], [[Mega Knight]], Royal Ghost, and Lava Hound, are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Monsters monster] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*The Inferno Dragon is the subject of an [[Emotes|Emote]].
*A [[Clone|cloned]] Inferno Dragon does not fall from the sky when deployed.
*The Inferno Dragon was featured in the winning deck of the [https://www.youtube.com/live/pRfrjMiHbQA?si=P2kVLJUlXH1SZoHm Clash Royale League 2021 Tournament], by a player called Mugi.

